  "steps": [
    {
      "step_id": "tile_sql_fund_aggregating_data.s01",
      "type": "explainer",
      "concept_ids": [
        "sql.aggregate_functions"
      ],
      "eyebrow": "Summary functions",
      "title": "Collapsing many rows into one number with aggregate functions",
      "lede": "So far your queries returned one row per record. Aggregate functions let you compute a single summary across all of them.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Aggregate functions compute a single result from a set of input values — many rows in, one value out. `COUNT(*)` counts every input row; `COUNT(delivery_time_minutes)` counts only the rows where that column is not null, so it skips the two undelivered QuickCart orders.",
          "role": "definition",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "sql.aggregate_functions"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "sql.aggregate_functions#f1",
              "sql.aggregate_functions#f2"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "sql.aggregate_functions#tb1",
              "sql.aggregate_functions#tb2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "The other four functions all ignore nulls. `SUM(delivery_time_minutes)` totals the non-null delivery times; `AVG` computes their arithmetic mean; `MIN` finds the shortest delivery; `MAX` finds the longest. One SELECT can compute all five at once, returning a single row of summary numbers.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "sql.aggregate_functions"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "sql.aggregate_functions#f3",
              "sql.aggregate_functions#f4",
              "sql.aggregate_functions#f5",
              "sql.aggregate_functions#f6"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "sql.aggregate_functions#tb3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "before_after",
          "block_id": "tile_sql_fund_aggregating_data.s01.ba",
          "before": {
            "type": "data_table",
            "asset_ref": {
              "asset_id": "ds_orders",
              "variant_id": null,
              "columns": [
                "order_id",
                "delivery_time_minutes"
              ]
            },
            "caption": "orders — one row per order, delivery_time_minutes shown (two NULLs)"
          },
          "after": {
            "type": "data_table",
            "result_of": {
              "runtime": "sql",
              "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_orders, COUNT(delivery_time_minutes) AS delivered_orders, SUM(delivery_time_minutes) AS total_minutes, AVG(delivery_time_minutes) AS avg_minutes, MIN(delivery_time_minutes) AS min_minutes, MAX(delivery_time_minutes) AS max_minutes FROM orders",
